      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve recalled that the setup in pkvm_init_percpu_fpu() is actually not for the guest itself, it is for pKVM to securely switch _from_ pVM to the host. Quoting the comment in arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/fpu/fpu.c: \"percpu_fpstate is used to reset the FPU hardware to its initial state when switching from pVM to host, preventing the host from accessing pVM\u0027s FPU contents.\"\n\nSo, is it correct to rely on this setup for our CPUID enforcement for pVM? Perhaps we should rely on the setup in pkvm_init_guest_fpu() instead?",
      "revId": "3c21acbf76409193ff0317ce340a0a40c556f43f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce3c4d3b_a1e226c9",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/init_finalise.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 521,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T20:01:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pkvm_init_cpuid() is called on every CPU, whereas is looks like it should be called just once?\n\nI see the comment says that it must be called after fpu initialization as it depends on some fpu setup. But what does it mean exactly, given that the fpu setup in pkvm_init_percpu_fpu() is per CPU, whereas the setup in pkvm_init_cpuid(), as far as I can see, is global?",
      "revId": "3c21acbf76409193ff0317ce340a0a40c556f43f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cadbd27c_7ea644b7",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/init_finalise.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 521,
      "author": {
        "id": 4222956
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T02:07:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "there is a check inside pkvm_init_cpuid():\n\n       if (pkvm_hyp-\u003ecpuid_nent)\n                return 0;\n\nso effectively it can be executed only once. The dependency comes from leaf (0xD) which calls xstate_get_guest_group_perm() using current-\u003egroup_leader-\u003ethread.fpu.",
      "parentUuid": "ce3c4d3b_a1e226c9",
      "revId": "3c21acbf76409193ff0317ce340a0a40c556f43f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac3991f6_44db1aa6",
